{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017me1jjm2LHfbvjZjh5A5pg","type":"tool_result","content":"internal/committer/codepath.go:13:// Refused: a .git segment, .gitmodules, everything under .ard/ (role, config\ninternal/committer/codepath.go:64:\tif strings.EqualFold(segs[len(segs)-1], \".gitmodules\") {\ninternal/committer/codepath_test.go:9:\t\t\".ard-input/12/issue.md\", \"a/.git/hooks/x\", \"a/.GIT/x\", \".gitmodules\", \"sub/.gitmodules\",\ninternal/worker/unit_test.go:87:\trejects := []Change{rc(\"a\"), rc(\".github/CODEOWNERS\"), rc(\".github/workflows/x.yml\"), rc(\".ard/config.yaml\"), rc(\".ard/workers/x/prompt.txt\"), rc(\".ard/8/plan.md\"), rc(\".env\"), rc(\"x/.git/config\"), rc(\".gitmodules\")}\ninternal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt:59:  .ard-input/, any path with a .git segment, and .gitmodules;\ninternal/roles/worker_engineer_test.go:74:\t\t\".github/\", \".gitmodules\", \"1,000\", \"256\", \"1 MiB\", \"symlink\", \"binary\", \"at run time\",\ndocs/proposal.md:300:5. **Guard the diff** after each agent or fix step, before anything leaves the host. The worktree belongs to the agent, so the guard never trusts its `.git`, config, index or attributes: git runs against the controller's own clone with a private index filled from the base commit (so `skip-worktree` and `assume-unchanged` hide nothing, and no planted filter, textconv, fsmonitor or hook runs), with its objects in a private temp directory (the clone is only read, so an agent cannot grow it); a worktree with a new or resized file over 1 MiB, or more than 256 of them, is held before anything is hashed. The scanned bytes are copied to a controller-private directory and the code lane commits the copies, so nothing can change a file between the scan and the commit. Close-out's changed-file listing uses the same hardened path. Paths under `.ard/<issue#>/` and `.ard-input/` belong to close-out and the loop and are left out. Everything else is checked, and any re