{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKx12vd7a9ijKpS2Vo2i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workers can no longer commit a `.gitattributes` file. `committer.CheckCodePath` now refuses one at any depth, case-insensitively, the same way it refuses `.gitmodules`. A rejection holds the job as `needs-human` with nothing pushed.\n\nMy first `go test ./...` run failed on one worker guard test. It expected \"and 5 more\" rejected paths, and the new rule adds one, so I changed the expected count to 6. The committer and worker packages pass on the rerun. I did not rerun the whole suite after that fix. All other packages passed in the first run, and gofmt reports nothing.\n\nI also added the refused and allowed cases to the committer and worker tests. The engineer prompt and its test now list `.gitattributes` as a rejected path. `docs/proposal.md` names the rule and says why: `linguist-generated` or `-diff` would collapse files in the GitHub PR diff.\n\nTwo things for the maintainers:\n- Workers can no longer make legitimate `.gitattributes` edits, such as line-ending config, without a human.\n- Adding `.gitattributes` to `merge.protected_paths` as well is a human config change, so I did not make it.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/142/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":611,"cache_read_input_tokens":17501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":611},"output_tokens":409,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc2666d3-9a26-416d-9c0f-d24ad7dd86cd","uuid":"9df6efec-b525-462b-b789-b955ba8b7b14","timestamp":"2026-11-23T13:36:20.887Z","request_id":"req_011ChKx12mTNFqNVy72raT4m"}
